#: device/block_operations.md
#: networking.md
msgid "Tools"
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "The module swings whatever is in the robot's currently selected inventory slot, exactly as a player holding that item would. A pickaxe mines stone, a shovel digs dirt, an axe chops wood, and an empty slot means no tool."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "The tool controls what can be broken and how long it takes to break it."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "Note that the tool will take damage and eventually break. Check its durability regularly if you'd rather repair it."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "Unbreakable blocks, such as bedrock, and blocks that would take longer than fifteen seconds cannot be broken."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "Gets the remaining durability of the tool in the currently selected inventory slot."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "Returns the remaining durability, or zero if the slot is empty or holds something that cannot take damage."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "Tries to break a block in the specified direction using the tool in the currently selected inventory slot. Collected blocks will be inserted starting after the currently selected inventory slot. If a slot is full, the next slot will be used. If the inventory has no space for the dropped block, it will drop into the world."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "`side`: the relative direction to break a block in. Optional, defaults to `front`. One of `front`, `up` or `down`."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "Returns whether the operation was successful."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
#: device/crafting.md
#: device/inventory_operations.md
#: device/scanner.md
#: device/tank_operations.md
#: device/transposer.md
msgid "Energy cost: `1`"
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "Tries to place a block in the specified direction. Blocks will be placed from the currently selected inventory slot. If the slot is empty, no block will be placed."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "`side`: the relative direction to place the block in. Optional, defaults to `front`. One of `front`, `up` or `down`."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "Device name: `BLKOPS`"
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
#: device/inventory_operations.md
msgid "Sides are numbered: `0` front, `1` up and `2` down."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "Takes one byte, the side to break a block in."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "Returns one byte, `1` if the operation was successful, `0` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "Takes one byte, the side to place the block in."
msgstr ""

#: device/block_operations.md
msgid "Returns four bytes, the remaining durability, or zero if the slot is empty or holds something that cannot take damage."
msgstr ""

