#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "File Import Export"
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Device name: `file_import_export`"
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Provided by the [file import/export card]({1})."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Exporting"
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Call `beginExportFile()` with a name, append the contents with `writeExportFile()`, then call `finishExportFile()`. Every user at the terminal is offered to save the file. Files are limited to 512 KiB."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Importing"
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Call `requestImportFile()` to prompt every user at the terminal for a file. Poll `beginImportFile()` until it returns the file's name and size; the first file a user picks wins, and the prompts on other clients are canceled. Then call `readImportFile()` until it returns nothing. `reset()` cancels either operation."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Methods fail with an error when called in the wrong order, or when the users canceled."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Begins exporting a file. Provide its contents with writeExportFile() and complete the export with finishExportFile(). Fails if the device is currently exporting or importing."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "`name`: the name of the file being exported."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Checks whether a requested file has arrived and, if so, starts reading it. Poll this after requestImportFile(). Fails if no import was requested, or every user canceled."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Returns a table with the file's `name` and `size`, or nothing while no file was picked yet."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Finishes the export and offers every user at the terminal to save the file. Fails if the device is not currently exporting."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Reads the next chunk of the file being imported. Fails if beginImportFile() did not succeed yet."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Returns up to 4 KiB of data, or nothing once the whole file was read."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Begins an import by prompting every user at the terminal to pick a file. Fails if the device is currently exporting or importing."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Returns whether anyone was prompted; `false` when nobody is using the terminal."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Cancels any export or import in progress and returns the device to its idle state."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "Appends data to the file being exported. Fails if the device is not currently exporting, or the file grows past 512 KiB."
msgstr ""

#: device/file_import_export.md
msgid "`data`: the data to append to the file being exported."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
