msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Device name: `fluid_handler`"
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Provided by any tank connected through a [bus interface]({1}), including cauldrons and the tanks of other mods. To move fluids between tanks, use a [transposer]({2}). Amounts are in millibuckets, a bucket being 1000."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "With several tanks connected, `find` may return any of them. To grab a specific one, give the bus interface in front of the one you want a name with a [wrench]({1}), and find it by that name instead."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Gets what is in the specified tank."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "`tank`: the number of the tank to look at."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Returns a table with the fluid `id`, such as `minecraft:water`, and the `amount` in millibuckets. Returns nothing for an empty tank."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Gets how much the specified tank can hold."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
#: device/tank_operations.md
#: device/transposer.md
msgid "Returns the capacity in millibuckets."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Gets how many tanks the container has."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Returns the number of tanks."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Device name: `FLUIDS`"
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Each container is listed separately. When several are connected, label the bus interface and pass both the label and `FLUIDS` to `OCFIND`, or check what `DEVS` lists."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Fluid ids are two bytes, low byte first; [`SYSTEM`]({1}) provides name lookup. An empty tank reads as fluid 0. Amounts are four bytes, low byte first."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Reads how many tanks the container has."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Returns one byte, the tank count, at most 255."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Reads a run of tanks in one call."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Ask for 1 to 42 tanks; more than that fails with `OCEARG`, since the reply would not fit. Reading stops at the end of the container, so asking for 42 tanks starting at 0 gives you as many as there are."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Takes two bytes, the tank to start at and how many tanks to read."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
#: device/tank_operations.md
#: device/transposer.md
msgid "Returns six bytes per tank: the fluid as two bytes and the amount as four bytes."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Reads how much the tank can hold."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
msgid "Takes one byte, the tank."
msgstr ""

#: device/fluid_handler.md
#: device/tank_operations.md
#: device/transposer.md
msgid "Returns four bytes, the capacity."
msgstr ""

