#: device/serial.md
msgid "Returns the number of sender collisions since the computer started."
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Device name: `SERIAL`"
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Counters are clamped to two bytes. Values wider than a byte are low byte first."
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Device order here may differ from the order the cards were installed in, so match them up by `getBaseAddress`."
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Reads the address this card is set to."
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Returns one byte, the address."
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Reads the baud rate the serial port is configured to."
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Returns four bytes, the baud rate in bits per second."
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Reads how many received bytes were lost because this computer did not read them in time."
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Returns two bytes, the count."
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Reads how often received data was corrupted by other endpoints sending at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Reads how often sent data was corrupted by other endpoints sending at the same time. A change after a send means it failed."
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Reads how often traffic arrived at a baud rate this port is not set to."
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Reads the I/O port this card's serial port registers start at, to tell cards apart."
msgstr ""

#: device/serial.md
msgid "Returns one byte, the port."
msgstr ""

